+### 0742 — A human ceremony has to be one board node, or the graph re-splits it (TASK-260728-3a2dnr, round 3)
+- ANOMALY: Round 2 described Ceremony C1 as one sitting, but no board element owned the sitting. The four grant-bearing tasks were ordered `apc34w` → {`3jloqy`, `dveo1o`}, so a `max_parallel = 1` scheduler produced **two** human stops with a full producer→reviewer cycle between them. Prose cannot batch a human interaction; only the DAG can. Recorded as ADR-028 and fixed by creating `TASK-260728-q5kjta`, the single up-front human-input node; `apc34w`, `3jloqy`, `dveo1o`, `ziprhs` are now unattended agent evidence tasks behind it, with their evidence obligations intact.
